course: dictionary
lesson: 366
title: A liquid that stops freezing
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Context means the words around a new word, and they often give you clues. «For example, antifreeze tastes sweet, so a child or a dog might drink it, but even a little can kill.» The sentence warns you that antifreeze is dangerous, so it must be a poison, not a sweet drink.
explain: Look at the other words too. Antifreeze goes in a car engine «to stop the water freezing in cold weather». Put those clues together: antifreeze is a liquid added to water so that it does not turn to ice.
explain: Test your meaning by putting it into the sentence. «Antifreeze stops water from freezing» makes sense, so you have understood the word. If your meaning does not fit, check the dictionary.
fact: Antifreeze is a liquid added to water to stop it freezing.
fact: Antifreeze is also used in car engines to help keep the engine cool.
fact: «Antifreeze» is poisonous, even though it tastes sweet, so it must be kept locked away.
fact: Antifreeze spills must be cleaned up, because animals and small children may drink them.
fact: Adding something to water lowers the temperature at which it freezes, just as salt does on icy roads.
exercise: What is antifreeze used for in a car? | To make the car go faster | *To stop the water in the engine freezing in cold weather | To make the engine freeze solid | To paint the outside of the car
exercise: «Antifreeze tastes sweet, so a child or a dog might drink it, but even a little can kill.» What does this tell you about antifreeze? | It tastes sour and is good for you | It is only used in summer | It is safe to drink | *It is poisonous and must be kept locked away
exercise: «Icefish carry natural antifreeze.» Which animal in these sentences carries natural antifreeze? | A seal | An emperor penguin | *Icefish | A dog
test: «Antifreeze» is added to water. What does this do to water in cold weather? | *It stops the water freezing | It makes the water turn to ice faster | It makes the water boil | It turns the water sweet
test: Why must spilled antifreeze be cleaned up quickly? | Because it helps plants grow | *Because animals and small children may drink it and be poisoned | Because it dries and leaves a smell | Because it makes a good drink for pets
exam: «Antifreeze» in «top up the antifreeze» means a liquid that stops water freezing, so what does «antifreeze poisoning» most likely mean? | Painting a car with antifreeze | *Being made ill by swallowing antifreeze | Being cured of a cold by antifreeze | A type of ice cream made with antifreeze
